From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Durr <jmdurr@live.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:49:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: efi: Power off the Inspiron 14 3420 through PSCI

The Dell Inspiron 14 3420 (SC8180XP) reboots when Linux powers it off
through the UEFI ResetSystem() runtime service. Don't register the EFI
power-off handler on it, so PSCI's SYSTEM_OFF turns it off.

[birk: the efi.c hunk of kernel.patch at a75479805a22, without its log
line, with the include in order and a comment on why.]
Link: https://github.com/jmdurr/dell-inspiron-3420-arm
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c
index 0ec90fd..fc81e9a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/efi.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/kmemleak.h>
 #include <linux/kthread.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/screen_info.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 
@@ -157,6 +158,10 @@ int __init efi_set_mapping_permissions(struct mm_struct *mm,
  */
 bool efi_poweroff_required(void)
 {
+	/* Its ResetSystem(EfiResetShutdown) reboots instead */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("dell,inspiron-3420-sc8180xp"))
+		return false;
+
 	return efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES);
 }
 
